{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1538551-how-do-you-represent-the-realm-in-your-campaign","id":1538551,"title":"How do you represent the realm in your campaign?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-13T22:32:53-07:00","id":1538551,"title":"How do you represent the realm in your campaign?","content":"(I don't speak English well so this was written with Google Translate, any errors please comment)<br /> I'm currently in a Dragon Blooded campaign with my cousin in 3e, which obviously involves the realm, and after reading the 3e manuals I realized that the representation of it is more nuanced than in 2e, it's not such a place. bad place to live and comparatively it is not on the highest scale of badness in the setting, this has caused the representation of the realm in my campaign to be much more positive than I expected and I was curious to know how other people represented it in their campaign. Please speak with respect and do not accuse anyone of advocating imperialism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28379-jose7057","name":"Jose7057","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T14:08:22-07:00","id":1538587,"title":"","content":"It tends to depend on the relation the group or, location they're in, has with it. Dynasts tend to view it as having some flaws, but otherwise a good place (moreso for Dragonblood Dynasts because of how much of the Realm is designed to benefit them.) Plus who they end up dealing with also helps, the island in our game that mostly deals with V'Neef merchants trading supplies and Peleps sailors handling pirates probably has a better opinion of the Scarlet Empire than the island that got assaulted by House Ledaal for various heresies against the immaculate order and housing anathema.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-23T03:19:14-07:00","id":1540932,"title":"","content":"I have a similar opinion regarding the kingdom and it's one of my favorite things about exalted, that the morals are more ambiguous and historically realistic than in most role-playing games, it's a shame there weren't more comments here, originally I thought I could get some ideas for my chronicle by listening to what others do in theirs, it is difficult to look for discussions that talk about the real world without the conversation ending up becoming tense and unnecessarily political, I always end up feeling uncomfortable and thinking that I am doing something wrong because want to play with a dynast","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28379-jose7057","name":"Jose7057","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-24T01:09:42-07:00","id":1540957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jose7057</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1538551-how-do-you-represent-the-realm-in-your-campaign?p=1540932#post1540932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a similar opinion regarding the kingdom and it's one of my favorite things about exalted, that the morals are more ambiguous and historically realistic than in most role-playing games, it's a shame there weren't more comments here, originally I thought I could get some ideas for my chronicle by listening to what others do in theirs, it is difficult to look for discussions that talk about the real world without the conversation ending up becoming tense and unnecessarily political, I always end up feeling uncomfortable and thinking that I am doing something wrong because want to play with a dynast</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say issues with wanting to play a Dynast are gonna come from why you want to play one. Like obviously if you're wanting to play because you want to play an upper class sociopath who treats the peasant population as a toy for their every whim and fear no consequence there will probably be issues. Whereas if you're just wanting to play a character that has support infrastructure, and is able to openly use their powers without fear of drawing so many murder targets on their head whenever they want to help people that's not gonna have an issue. Not to mention The Realm is an interesting place to play about in, acknowledging that it isn't a great place by real world standards doesn't mean that you're a bad person if you want to explore it from the perspective of someone its designed to benefit and serve without the focus of wanting to see it all torn down to fit a better real world governmental style. <br /> <br /> Talk to your group about wanting to play it. Lot of people have fun with the dragonblood academies from what I've heard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-24T04:18:25-07:00","id":1540958,"title":"","content":"You represented my point of view on this topic well, the kingdom is one of the most interesting places I have seen in a faith fantasy world and I really love it as a setting, it is not perfect by modern standards, but let's be honest with the fact. that no place in creation would be suitable according to current paradigms, the lunars have hundreds of empires as cruel as the kingdom, in addition to turning relatively peaceful societies into weapons against the kingdom, the bull of the north is Genghis Khan's exalted version, and the people themselves mortals are responsible for the existence of places like nexus and great forks, I think what bothers me the most is that this topic is only touched on when it is with the realm (I wrote this with the translator so it may have errors)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28379-jose7057","name":"Jose7057","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}